  "query_preview": "..The sky was clear this morning as the thick cloud\ncover that was over the area yesterday has moved on east. Water\nvapor imagery showed an upper low NW of Vegas. This upper low\nwill continue to bring below normal high temperatures today and\ntomorrow while also bringing gusty SW winds and elevated fire \nweather conditions today. Near normal high temperatures to close\nout May on Sunday then June starts with slightly above normal \nhighs and triple-digit highs for lower deserts. Moisture seep\ninto the eastern areas next week will bring a chance of\nafternoon and evening showers and thunderstorms mainly east of\nTucson Wed and Thu. \n\n8-14 day outlooks (June 5-11)\nTemperature: Leaning above normal\nPrecipitation: Leaning above normal most of area",
